Unannotated empty dict with int-key subscript-assigns: the dict is
built with the actual key/value element types (via creation-time
look-ahead from the first d[k] = v, or a first-assign rebuild) so
distinct int keys aren't lossily coerced to the default str key type.
See dict-int-key-loop for the in-loop case.
